      "startDescription": "16 August 1991. The Ukrainian SSR is the second largest republic of the Union: 52 million people, the Donbas, the black-earth farmland, the Black Sea Fleet and the third largest nuclear arsenal in the world. A year ago the Supreme Soviet proclaimed state sovereignty, and the Chairman of the Rada, Leonid Kravchuk, carefully steers the republic between Moscow and Rukh. In three days Moscow will try to stop the collapse of the Union by force. Can Ukraine become an independent state, and what kind of state will it be?",
